=== Part 3: human-like demographies, exact B&L eq (3) (no simulation; effects below sim resolution) ===
  annual survival s=0.96 (Tg=25 y); constant-demography k/mu per step = 0.040
  (a) symmetric exponential growth/decline cycle, rate r per year, constant feasible survival:
     r=0.005/yr: range x3.27; k/mu = 0.03999; standardized ks = k/(1-s) = 0.99970; theory 1-(s/(1-s))(cosh r-1) = 0.99970
     r=0.016/yr: range x3.22; k/mu = 0.03988; standardized ks = k/(1-s) = 0.99693; theory 1-(s/(1-s))(cosh r-1) = 0.99693
     r=0.030/yr: range x3.22; k/mu = 0.03957; standardized ks = k/(1-s) = 0.98920; theory 1-(s/(1-s))(cosh r-1) = 0.98920
     r=0.039/yr: range x4.58; k/mu = 0.03927; standardized ks = k/(1-s) = 0.98175; theory 1-(s/(1-s))(cosh r-1) = 0.98175
  (b) Day's window: ONE-WAY growth 2.5->8.2 (1.6%/yr, 75 y). Instantaneous eventual-fixer arrival rate relative to mu(1-s):
      growth rate 0.0160/yr; births/N = 1 - s/(1+r) = 0.0551 vs constant 0.0400; ratio = 1.377
      total excess over the whole episode, in units of U: s*ln(N_end/N_start) = 1.140 (one-off, finite)
  (c) growth then catastrophic bottleneck (all adults die), 75 y growth at 1.6%/yr, s=0.96 (B&L eq 14 type):
      k/mu per step = 0.0675; ks = 1.688  (positive, contrived: a cycle that kills every adult once per 75 y)
  (d) B&L 2-state, N2/N1 = 3.28: scan survival (s11,s22,s12,s21 in [0,1], feasibility s21<=N1/N2), alpha=.5; ks range:
      min ks = 0.590 at (s11,s22,s12,s21)=(np.float64(1.0), np.float64(1.0), np.float64(0.0), np.float64(0.3))
      max ks = 1.695 at (s11,s22,s12,s21)=(np.float64(1.0), np.float64(1.0), np.float64(1.0), np.float64(0.0))
      biologically ordered subset (survival higher when growing, s12>=s11,s22>=s21): 
      ordered range of ks: [0.833, 1.695]

